1. CreateLabourDetail: save wrench time into AdjHrs

Add using System.Globalization; at the top of the file. Inside the try, right after string hrsReqd = ...;, add:

csharp
// Wrench time = (HrsReqd in minutes) / NON_PRODUCTIVE_ADJUSTMENT, stored as H:MM in AdjHrs
var npaText = await _dbConnection.QueryFirstOrDefaultAsync<string>(
    "SELECT Value FROM SBCES.CESSETTINGS WHERE Parameter = 'NON_PRODUCTIVE_ADJUSTMENT'",
    transaction: transaction);

decimal npa = decimal.TryParse((npaText ?? "1").Replace(',', '.'),
                  NumberStyles.Any, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out var parsedNpa) && parsedNpa > 0
              ? parsedNpa : 1m;

int.TryParse(model.LabourHrs?.ToString(), out var reqHours);
int.TryParse(model.LabourMins?.ToString(), out var reqMins);

int wrenchMinutes = (int)Math.Round((reqHours * 60 + reqMins) / npa, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero);
string wrenchTime = $"{wrenchMinutes / 60}:{wrenchMinutes % 60:D2}";   // 2:00 / 1.2 = 100 min -> "1:40"

In the parameters object, replace model.AdjHrs, with:

csharp
AdjHrs = wrenchTime,

If AdjHrs on the model is a string, also set model.AdjHrs = wrenchTime; so the grid shows it right away. The same change is needed in the second CreateLabourDetail copy you pasted, and in any update/edit action. Otherwise edited rows will keep stale wrench time.

2. STEP 4: read wrench time from EmployeeLabour

This is for GetTotalCostInMakeVsBuyEstimatesWithDetails. AdjustedHours stays numeric, so the 1:33 parse error does not return. Cost still uses TimeAddition.

sql
WITH LabourData AS (
    SELECT
        EL.Task,
        EL.LabourDefn,
        EL.CostCentre AS CC,

        -- Required hours (H:MM) converted to decimal hours
        (CAST(ISNULL(LEFT(EL.HrsReqd, CHARINDEX(':', EL.HrsReqd) - 1), 0) AS DECIMAL(18,2)) +
         CAST(ISNULL(SUBSTRING(EL.HrsReqd, CHARINDEX(':', EL.HrsReqd) + 1, LEN(EL.HrsReqd)), 0) AS DECIMAL(18,2)) / 60) AS DecimalHrs,

        -- Wrench time: stored AdjHrs (H:MM) converted to decimal hours
        ISNULL(CASE WHEN CHARINDEX(':', EL.AdjHrs) > 0
             THEN TRY_CAST(LEFT(EL.AdjHrs, CHARINDEX(':', EL.AdjHrs) - 1) AS DECIMAL(18,6))
                + TRY_CAST(SUBSTRING(EL.AdjHrs, CHARINDEX(':', EL.AdjHrs) + 1, 10) AS DECIMAL(18,6)) / 60.0
             ELSE TRY_CAST(REPLACE(EL.AdjHrs, ',', '.') AS DECIMAL(18,6))
        END, 0) AS WrenchHrs,

        -- Hours used for cost: TimeAddition, same as Oracle
        ISNULL(TRY_CAST(REPLACE(CAST(EL.TimeAddition AS VARCHAR(30)), ',', '.') AS DECIMAL(18,6)), 0) AS CostHrs,

        CAST(NULLIF(EL.Usage, '') AS DECIMAL(18,2)) AS UsagePercent,
        ISNULL((SELECT TOP 1 ES.RatePerHour FROM CES.SBCES.EmployeeSalaries ES
                WHERE ES.WageGroup = (SELECT TOP 1 EC.WageGroup FROM CES.SBCES.EmplClass EC
                                      WHERE EC.LabourDefn LIKE '%' + EL.LabourDefn + '%')), 0) AS RatePerHour
    FROM SBCES.EmployeeLabour EL
    WHERE EL.LinkNumber = @Id AND EL.TypeId = 'MB'
)
SELECT
    ISNULL(Task, 'Unnamed Task') AS Task,
    ISNULL(LabourDefn, 'N/A') AS LabourDefinition,
    ISNULL(CC, '') AS CC,
    COUNT(*) AS Count,
    SUM(DecimalHrs) AS Hours,
    SUM(DecimalHrs * UsagePercent / 100) AS EffectiveHours,
    -- Wrench hours x Usage%, rounded to whole minutes, returned as decimal hours (numeric)
    CAST(ROUND(SUM(WrenchHrs * 60 * UsagePercent / 100), 0) / 60.0 AS DECIMAL(18,6)) AS AdjustedHours,
    AVG(RatePerHour) AS RatePerHour,
    SUM(CostHrs * UsagePercent / 100 * RatePerHour) AS TotalCost
FROM LabourData
GROUP BY Task, LabourDefn, CC
ORDER BY Task
